{"type":"text","timestamp":1785550913960,"sessionID":"ses_045020059ffetDN2TLGi6CMad5","part":{"id":"prt_fbb209f80001M3KO4y72BXWjoC","messageID":"msg_fbb2093ca001P6MlfLfRdxP9kJ","sessionID":"ses_045020059ffetDN2TLGi6CMad5","type":"text","text":"Done. The Brazilian Soccer MCP server is implemented, tested, and verified — **216 tests pass** and the stdio server answers real MCP JSON-RPC calls.\n\n## What was built\n\n**Package `soccer_mcp/`** + `server.py` stdio entry point (FastMCP, 19 tools):\n- `normalize.py` — team-name canonicalization across all five naming conventions (`Palmeiras-SP`, `América - MG`, `Athletico-PR`, `Vasco Da Gama RJ`, `Sport Club Corinthians Paulista`) with ~100 curated aliases, competition synonym resolution, ISO/Brazilian/datetime parsing, UTF-8 handling, and a 24-pair derby table (Fla-Flu, Gre-Nal, …)\n- `data.py` — loads all 6 CSVs into a deduplicated 16,732-match unified table + 18,207-player table\n- `queries.py` / `formatting.py` / `tools_api.py` — structured query layer → spec-format text rendering → flat tool functions\n- `mcp_server.py` — FastMCP wiring with tool descriptions from docstrings\n\n**Data-quality fixes discovered while testing against ground truth:**\n- Cross-source dedupe keyed on `(competition, season, home, away)` — dates are unreliable (±1 day timezone drift) and scores occasionally conflict; calculated 2019 standings now reproduce reality exactly (Flamengo 90 pts, correct relegation zone)\n- COVID-19 overflow: 2020-season matches played Jan–Mar 2021 reassigned to season 2020 (2020 champion Flamengo, 71 pts ✓)\n- Removed the phantom 0-0 for the cancelled 2016 Chapecoense–Atlético-MG fixture (LaMia disaster) and a mislabeled state-championship row\n\n**Testing (216 passed, ~3s):**\n- 135 unit tests (normalization, loading/dedupe, queries)\n- 46 Gherkin BDD scenarios via pytest-bdd, structured Given/When/Then per the spec's testing approach, including the spec's two verbatim scenarios\n- 11 MCP integration tests through an in-memory FastMCP client (tool registration, calls, error propagation)\n- 24 sample questions from the spec encoded as a parametrized test\n\n**Success criteria met:** all 6 CSVs loadable/queryable, cross-file queries work, lookups 1–20 ms / aggregates 2–7 ms (limits: 2 s/5 s), and `python server.py` passes a real stdio MCP handshake + `tools/call` smoke test.","time":{"start":1785550905216,"end":1785550913955}}}
